Two balls, X and Y, move along a horizontal frictionless surface, as shown from above in Fig. 4.1. {{figure:fig_4_1}}

Ball X has a mass of $3.0\,\mathrm{kg}$ and a velocity of $4.0\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ in a direction at angle $\theta$ to a line AB. Ball Y has a mass of $2.5\,\mathrm{kg}$ and a velocity of $4.8\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ in a direction at angle $\theta$ to the line AB.

The balls collide and stick together. After colliding, the balls have a velocity of $3.7\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ along the line AB on the horizontal surface, as shown in Fig. 4.2. {{figure:fig_4_2}}

